        24["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Living Crystal</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Extends the existing endless<br />world, inventory, clock and<br />commands. New-world<br />geography, local indexed<br />heat/light, damage, tending,<br />renewable wild colonies,<br />protected material<br />condition/storage/transfer,<br />and the first dormant-machine<br />repair. Original texture-pack<br />buildings gain physical<br />shutters/fans and condition<br />marks in the existing row<br />renderer. Legacy<br />terrain/rules and saves are<br />retained.</div>"]
        style 24 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        25["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Layered World</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Coordinates and key packing<br />(x, y, z), tile rules as data<br />(TILE_INFO), and chunked<br />terrain: the forest surface<br />at z = 0 from noise octaves,<br />solid geology below with one<br />shaft per chunk. Chunks are<br />generated lazily and<br />LRU-cached; player edits<br />(richness mods), per-layer<br />fog and the holes between<br />layers live outside the<br />cache. Explored chunks and<br />observed resource types have<br />derived spatial indexes,<br />including one/two-unit<br />reserve masks that remove<br />exhausted deposits from<br />searches; Map-compatible prop<br />mutation epochs invalidate<br />charger candidates.</div>"]
        style 25 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        26["<div style='font-weight: bold'>State and Saves</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>createState() builds the<br />state; serialize/deserialize<br />write and validate a JSON<br />save (its format is<br />WORLD_FORMAT in format.js,<br />frozen so every world is<br />kept; saves from format 10 on<br />load, and the browser sets<br />aside, never overwrites, one<br />it can't read). state.events<br />is transient and never saved.</div>"]
        style 26 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        27["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Simulation Step</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>step(s, dt): production,<br />logistics, abundance income<br />and battery; movement and fog<br />reveal. Browser and AUTO<br />hosts enable cumulative solo<br />production after Logistics:<br />grouped rates, cached<br />counts/mastery, command/query<br />settlements, and buffer<br />snapshots at saves or rate<br />changes. Visual events query<br />nearby tile buckets.<br />Cultivation runs local<br />environment deadlines at<br />250ms in the same canonical<br />step. Battery intervals<br />support quiet-tick batching<br />and reuse nearby charger<br />candidates with exact range<br />and daylight checks. Reveal<br />compares exact circle row<br />intervals and visits newly<br />covered edges. Resource<br />streams settle together with<br />targeted manual balance<br />updates. Variable-step/shared<br />callers and extreme<br />arithmetic retain the legacy<br />economy.</div>"]
        style 27 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        28["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Actions</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Harvest (gather deposits on<br />the surface, dig rock<br />underground), Trail sweep<br />targets, collect, and build;<br />plus travel between layers<br />through holes (dig down from<br />the forest, climb up through<br />the ceiling, drop through<br />holes and shafts). All work<br />on the player's own layer.</div>"]
        style 28 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        29["<div style='font-weight: bold'>AUTO Brain</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>nextIntent(s, mind): legal<br />player actions from explored<br />terrain, remembered<br />observations, visible mine<br />glints, own resources and<br />public rules. Integer A*<br />treats unseen underground<br />rock as an assumption and<br />replans after normal<br />revelation, without<br />inspecting hidden geology.<br />Unseen chargers, ladders,<br />shores and tunnel props<br />cannot steer decisions.<br />Prices building repayment<br />against required upgrades;<br />mining is a fallback only<br />when surface acquisition is<br />unavailable, includes passive<br />income and return travel and<br />targets useful observed<br />finds. Waits at Embark, and<br />never spends Insight in<br />shared worlds. Selected known<br />chargers alone authorize<br />charging decisions. Manual<br />holds share AUTO cadence.<br />Pure: mind caches<br />observations and routes.</div>"]
        style 29 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        30["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Stockpile</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>What you own as piles around<br />home, on a logarithmic scale:<br />one pile per unit of the two<br />leading digits (at most 18<br />per resource), each power of<br />ten its own kind; from 10^7 a<br />pile covers a square of tiles<br />one wider per power, as far<br />as its slot allows. Home<br />ground is a square laid out<br />like a town: roads cross in<br />the middle and each resource<br />owns a block with fixed slots<br />(the leading digit in the<br />corner by the crossroads, the<br />second along the outer<br />edges), so nothing stands<br />outside home ground or on<br />another pile. Pure: only a<br />picture of the inventory.</div>"]
        style 30 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        31["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Catalog</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Everything that exists in the<br />game, by the id a texture<br />pack knows it by: tiles,<br />resources, buildings, the<br />wanderer, marks, buttons,<br />upgrades, perks and colours,<br />each with what it does and<br />the slots a pack can fill.<br />Built from the other content<br />tables, so a new tile or<br />upgrade can't go<br />undocumented.</div>"]
        style 31 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
        32["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Economy and Upgrades</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: JavaScript]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Content tables, costs and<br />multipliers, and one registry<br />of every purchase (tools,<br />refineries, the Abundance<br />Engine, unlocks, perks) that<br />buying, the progression map<br />and the sheet all share; the<br />ledger (income lines,<br />spending at today's prices,<br />payback in seconds of your<br />own income). Stoneworks<br />supplies a non-stacking<br />same-owner quarry bonus<br />within two tiles. A derived<br />tile index caches service<br />links per layout; both scalar<br />and event economies use<br />instance rates. Experimental<br />solo depots use an eight-tile<br />same-owner/layer collection<br />index; overlapping depots<br />never duplicate transfers.<br />Also embark/prestige and the<br />goal track.</div>"]
        style 32 fill:#3f7d3a,stroke:#2c5728,color:#ffffff
